**How to implement.** The constructor windows' Items panel reads the app's item models with the kit's snapshots, and an item added in a real window is a kit file (the S7.2 brief; the S7.1 mapper's request: offer `AppContext.itemModels`; .spec-md §0.1 `Program.fs`; 001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: each constructor window's seed (steps 154, 189) threads `itemModels = context.itemModels.overlaidWith opened.overlay` (steps 220, 222) by record update beside `catalogueImports`; `itemIds` stays `initWith`'s `ItemIdProvider.system` (step 239), and the photo picker is the system dialog the view opens (step 241). The docs of `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that their Items panel reads the app's item models. No other seam changes. (2) Tests, in `KitWindowTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: an item added in a constructor window is a kit file with its model's snapshot, and the window reopened lists it`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitWindowTests")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152): pressing `flowItemsStep`, `addItemButton`, the circular polarizer's offer, setting `newItemLabelField`'s text to `CPL1` and pressing `addItemConfirmButton` shows CPL1's `kitItemRow`; the kit's folder holds `CPL1.item-json` and `library/33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b@v1.item-model-json`; the window closed, a second `MainConstructorWindow` over the same folder opened again through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) shows CPL1's `kitItemRow` once `flowItemsStep` is pressed. The windows' other consumers keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the windows are wired, a constructor window's Items panel MUST offer the app's item models over the kit's snapshots and record an added item in the kit's folder with its model's snapshot; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: an item added in a constructor window is a kit file with its model's snapshot, and the window reopened lists it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
